# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.DS_Store

# Job-application working files. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC on GitHub, and anything
# committed under docs/ is world-readable. These files carry internal J&J
# system names, internal cost models, candid self-assessment and targeted
# positioning — none of which should ever be published. Keep them local.
docs/interview-prep-*.md
# Targeted cover letters name the company being applied to. Publishing one tells
# every other reader of this public repo exactly where else the search is aimed.
docs/cover-letter-*.md
# Blanket: no PDF under docs/ is ever meant to be published. A targeted CV
# saved under a generic filename slipped past the specific rule once already.
docs/*.pdf

# Candid self-assessment of what the CV is missing, plus team composition and
# notes on what was deliberately withheld. A recruiter reading this reads the
# weaknesses before the record.
#
# NOTE: a rule here does NOTHING for a file git already tracks — the index wins
# over .gitignore. Both this file and docs/cover-letter-airbnb-sr-manager.md were
# listed here yet still published, because they had been committed first. If you
# add a pattern for a file that already exists in the repo, you must also run:
#   git rm --cached <path>
/CV_GAPS.md